WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.158
Must a caring friend solve everything?

00:00:03.158 --> 00:00:06.316
Care also needs sustainable limits.

00:00:06.316 --> 00:00:09.474
Peer-support guidance emphasizes listening and suitable help.

00:00:09.474 --> 00:00:12.632
Respect choice and know when more resources are needed.

00:00:12.632 --> 00:00:15.789
Friends and professionals have different roles.

00:00:15.789 --> 00:00:22.105
Ask what is needed right now.

00:00:22.105 --> 00:00:28.421
Consider what you can realistically offer.

00:00:28.421 --> 00:00:34.737
Connect a network of support.

00:00:34.737 --> 00:00:41.053
The network illustrates support, not a predicted outcome.

00:00:41.053 --> 00:00:44.211
Being caring does not require constant availability.

00:00:44.211 --> 00:00:47.368
Avoid promises you cannot safely keep.

00:00:47.368 --> 00:00:50.526
Seek reliable adults when safety is at risk.

00:00:50.526 --> 00:00:56.842
Listen together or find an appropriate helper.

00:00:56.842 --> 00:01:03.158
Clarify availability and later contact.

00:01:03.158 --> 00:01:06.316
Let supporters have support of their own.

00:01:06.316 --> 00:01:09.474
Companionship can matter beyond solving a problem.

00:01:09.474 --> 00:01:12.632
Another reliable connection offers another possibility.

00:01:12.632 --> 00:01:15.789
A network reaches wider than one rope.
